    "question": "Mike gets paid 100 dollars a week.  He decides to spend half of that at an arcade.  He spends 10 dollars at the arcade on food and uses the rest on arcade tokens. He can play for 1 hour for $8. How many minutes can he play?",
    "gold": "300",
    "answer": "He spent 100*.5=$<<100*.5=50>>50 at the arcade.\nHe uses 50-10=$<<50-10=40>>40 on tokens\nHe can play 40/8=<<40/8=5>>5 hours\nThere are 60 minutes in an hour so he can play 5*60=<<5*60=300>>300 minutes\n#### 300"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many minutes Mike can play at the arcade, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate how much money Mike spends at the arcade.\n2. Determine how much money Mike spends on arcade tokens.\n3. Calculate how many hours Mike can play with the money he has left after buying food.\n4. Convert the number of hours into minutes.\n\nStep 1: Calculate how much money Mike spends at the arcade.\nMike gets paid $100 a week and spends half of that at the arcade.\n\\[ \\text{Money spent at the arcade} = \\frac{100}{2} = 50 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nStep 2: Determine how much money Mike spends on arcade tokens.\nMike spends $10 on food, so the remaining money is:\n\\[ \\text{Money left for tokens} = 50 - 10 = 40 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nStep 3: Calculate how many hours Mike can play with the money he has left after buying food.\nMike can play for 1 hour for $8. Therefore, the number of hours he can play with $40 is:\n\\[ \\text{Number of hours} = \\frac{40}{8} = 5 \\text{ hours} \\]\n\nStep 4: Convert the number of hours into minutes.\nSince there are 60 minutes in an hour, the total number of minutes Mike can play is:\n\\[ \\text{Total minutes} = 5 \\times 60 = 300 \\text{ minutes} \\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[ \\boxed{300} \\]",
